- The type T requires Clone because we want to produce owned values in the output Vec<HashMap<...>>; if you want to avoid cloning you can change the input type and ownership accordingly.
- If you specifically need rayon-utils for some multi-way zipping beyond two sequences, it can be added; for two sequences Rayon’s built-in par_iter().zip(...) is sufficient and efficient.

