/// Resets the row index of a table and converts the existing index values into new columns.
///
/// # Arguments
/// * `table` - The input table with an existing index
///
/// # Returns
/// A new table with:
/// - Reset row index (0, 1, 2, ...)
/// - Original index values as a new column named "original_index"
///
/// # Example
