/// and returns them as a new list.
///
/// # Arguments
///
/// * `json_data` - A JSON string containing a list of items
/// * `attribute_path` - A JMESPath expression specifying which attribute to extract
///
/// # Returns
///
/// * `Result<String, Box<dyn Error>>` - A JSON string containing the extracted values,
///   or an error if parsing or matching fails
///
/// # Example
///
